WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:03.236 align:start size:94% position:6% line:0%
♫♫

00:00:03.236 --> 00:00:06.339 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hello, everybody, welcome to
corrections for week --

00:00:06.339 --> 00:00:10.043
for the week of June 14th,

00:00:10.043 --> 00:00:11.878 align:start size:94% position:6%
and we´re just going
to get started

00:00:11.878 --> 00:00:14.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
because we have quite a --
we have quite a few.

00:00:16.850 --> 00:00:18.151 size:84% position:42%
A couple of weeks back,

00:00:18.151 --> 00:00:22.188 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said that I bought
a toy at Kmart,

00:00:22.188 --> 00:00:26.393
a bunch of people said
all of those stores are closed,

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.528 size:84% position:42%
they´re not all closed.

00:00:28.528 --> 00:00:31.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
However,
I did mispronounce it.

00:00:31.431 --> 00:00:34.768
It is not Kmart, it is Kmarts

00:00:34.768 --> 00:00:37.904 size:78% position:39%
with an S at the end.

00:00:37.904 --> 00:00:41.107 align:start size:94% position:6%
The one that I keep
putting on Kroger.

00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:43.576 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s Kmarts.

00:00:43.576 --> 00:00:46.146 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said last week
during corrections,

00:00:46.146 --> 00:00:48.048 align:start size:94% position:6%
and again, it is
a recurring problem

00:00:48.048 --> 00:00:50.150 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I make errors
in the body of correction

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:52.919 align:start size:94% position:6%
that I then have
to loop back on.

00:00:52.919 --> 00:00:56.556 size:81% position:41%
I said the "gig" is up

00:00:56.556 --> 00:00:58.124
when referring to a teacher

00:00:58.124 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
discovering
that a group of students

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.762 align:start size:94% position:6%
were using their calculators
to spell boobs.

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:04.964 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said the teacher
would say the gig is up.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:07.634 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of you

00:01:07.634 --> 00:01:11.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
so quickly, I would imagine
your keyboards

00:01:11.071 --> 00:01:14.741 align:start size:94% position:6%
are melting with the speed
you pounded in it

00:01:14.741 --> 00:01:16.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
is the jig is up.

00:01:16.509 --> 00:01:18.978 size:88% position:44%
It is not the gig is up.

00:01:18.978 --> 00:01:22.315
I am aware of the jig is up.

00:01:22.315 --> 00:01:25.285
That is not what I was saying.

00:01:25.285 --> 00:01:27.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
A gig is a job,
I know you know that,

00:01:27.887 --> 00:01:31.191
but time and time again, you
tell me things you know I know.

00:01:34.294 --> 00:01:36.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
What I was saying
is that the teacher,

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.566
upon seeing this was done.

00:01:41.701 --> 00:01:45.038 size:84% position:42%
For real, she was like,
why am I doing this?

00:01:45.038 --> 00:01:46.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m trying to teach
these kids math

00:01:46.606 --> 00:01:48.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they´re just using
their calculators

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:52.078 align:start size:94% position:6%
to, you know,
write dirty words?

00:01:52.078 --> 00:01:53.880 align:start size:94% position:6%
I quit.

00:01:53.880 --> 00:01:57.984 align:start size:94% position:6%
The gig...is up.

00:01:57.984 --> 00:02:00.887
It´s not always the idiom.

00:02:03.990 --> 00:02:08.094
Yesterday´s "Closer Look"
I mentioned the Swiss president

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:12.198
sort of introduced Putin and...

00:02:12.198 --> 00:02:14.134 size:81% position:41%
Not Trump, oh, my God.

00:02:14.134 --> 00:02:15.635 align:start size:94% position:6%
Well, I think
it´s still Trump.

00:02:18.538 --> 00:02:21.508
A couple of Swiss viewers said,
hey, we don´t have a president.

00:02:21.508 --> 00:02:25.178 align:start size:94% position:6%
What we have
is a Swiss president --

00:02:25.178 --> 00:02:29.315
Sorry, it´s the president
of the Swiss Confederation.

00:02:29.315 --> 00:02:32.685 align:start size:94% position:6%
There is a federal council
of sorts

00:02:32.685 --> 00:02:35.889 size:81% position:41%
of seven Swiss leaders

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:38.625
with a rotating president.

00:02:38.625 --> 00:02:40.293
It has to be consensus, though,

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:43.563 align:start size:94% position:6%
for the one
representative president

00:02:43.563 --> 00:02:45.899 align:start size:94% position:6%
to speak.

00:02:45.899 --> 00:02:47.267
So it´s not one, it´s seven.

00:02:47.267 --> 00:02:50.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
I think the best way to think
about Swiss politics,

00:02:50.603 --> 00:02:52.839 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess, would be
it´s not like

00:02:52.839 --> 00:02:56.176 align:start size:94% position:6%
a knife with one blade,
it´s like a knife with a fork

00:02:56.176 --> 00:03:00.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
and a spoon and a blade
and a little saw and tweezers.

00:03:07.120 --> 00:03:10.256 size:78% position:39%
We´ll keep in Europe.

00:03:10.256 --> 00:03:14.260 align:start size:94% position:6%
I talked about
a Finnish mountain gnome.

00:03:14.260 --> 00:03:17.230 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was told that Finland
is without mountains,

00:03:17.230 --> 00:03:19.866 size:84% position:42%
is a very flat country.

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:25.038
I should have said a Finnish
forest gnome and I am sorry.

00:03:25.038 --> 00:03:28.875
I, however, was told that my
Finnish accent was fantastic.

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.781
A lot of people asked about it,
I addressed it last week,

00:03:34.781 --> 00:03:38.218 align:start size:94% position:6%
how we censor, even though
it´s not on television,

00:03:38.218 --> 00:03:43.056
curse words are censored
in the body of this piece.

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:45.658
And I said that I did not know

00:03:45.658 --> 00:03:49.596 align:start size:94% position:6%
and was not even aware
that we beep the curse words

00:03:49.596 --> 00:03:53.866 align:start size:94% position:6%
and people said it´s not beep,
it´s bleep.

00:03:53.866 --> 00:03:55.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
You don´t beep a curse word,
you bleep it.

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:57.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I thought maybe as
an experiment

00:03:57.337 --> 00:03:58.972 size:78% position:39%
we could just try it.

00:03:58.972 --> 00:04:01.374
So for anyone who felt the need
to tell me that,

00:04:01.374 --> 00:04:02.842 size:75% position:38%
go [bleep] yourself.

00:04:02.842 --> 00:04:04.978 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did we hear?

00:04:04.978 --> 00:04:06.079 align:start size:94% position:6%
What did we hear?

00:04:06.079 --> 00:04:09.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
Was it a beep?
Was it a bleep?

00:04:13.319 --> 00:04:15.955 size:88% position:44%
7-Eleven makes slurpies.

00:04:15.955 --> 00:04:19.559 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said slushies.

00:04:19.559 --> 00:04:21.894 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s a mistake
I want to correct.

00:04:21.894 --> 00:04:23.529 align:start size:94% position:6%
By the way,

00:04:23.529 --> 00:04:26.766
if you go to 7-Eleven and say
slushies, it´s going to be fine.

00:04:30.203 --> 00:04:33.940 align:start size:94% position:6%
They´re not going
to get the manager.

00:04:33.940 --> 00:04:37.977
Applebee´s, I was a little
critical of their slogan,

00:04:37.977 --> 00:04:40.480 align:start size:94% position:6%
"eating good
in the neighborhood."

00:04:40.480 --> 00:04:41.881 align:start size:94% position:6%
And the fact
that there aren´t Applebee´s

00:04:41.881 --> 00:04:44.317 size:84% position:42%
in little neighborhoods

00:04:44.317 --> 00:04:48.221 align:start size:94% position:6%
in a bunch of suburban viewers
said that they do,

00:04:48.221 --> 00:04:51.758
in fact, they might be at malls,
but they are nearby

00:04:51.758 --> 00:04:53.726 size:81% position:41%
and they consider that
in their neighborhood.

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I am sorry

00:04:55.928 --> 00:04:57.430 size:75% position:38%
that you live there.

00:04:57.430 --> 00:05:01.100 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m kidding.

00:05:01.100 --> 00:05:02.869 size:88% position:44%
I grew up in the suburbs

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:06.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
I would have killed
to have an Applebee´s.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:13.046
Last, we get a closer look,

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:15.381 align:start size:94% position:6%
we said a cappuccino
is a latte with extra foam

00:05:15.381 --> 00:05:18.951
and a lot of coffee lovers

00:05:18.951 --> 00:05:22.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
told us that was totally wrong
and any time,

00:05:22.622 --> 00:05:23.890
while we did make a mistake,

00:05:23.890 --> 00:05:25.425 align:start size:94% position:6%
any time,
if you can make a mistake

00:05:25.425 --> 00:05:27.927 align:start size:94% position:6%
that gets you to engage
with coffee lovers,

00:05:27.927 --> 00:05:31.764
it´s a worthwhile mistake.

00:05:31.764 --> 00:05:33.433 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just to talk with those
who have coffee,

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:37.203
but this is -- I realized
what happened, which is

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.439
Sal Gentile wrote that joke,

00:05:39.439 --> 00:05:42.275 align:start size:94% position:6%
and Sal doesn´t know
fancy coffee.

00:05:42.275 --> 00:05:44.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
We shouldn´t have --
we should have fact checked

00:05:44.677 --> 00:05:47.313
the minute Sal started talking
about lattes and cappuccinos.

00:05:47.313 --> 00:05:53.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
A key -- Sal makes
his own coffee in a pan.

00:05:53.186 --> 00:05:57.190 align:start size:94% position:6%
He just shakes some Sanka
into a pan,

00:05:57.190 --> 00:06:01.928 align:start size:94% position:6%
put some water,
fries it over an open flame,

00:06:01.928 --> 00:06:04.297 align:start size:94% position:6%
drains it through
his meds cap.

00:06:09.202 --> 00:06:11.037 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean...

00:06:11.037 --> 00:06:13.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I mean, to put it
in Dennis Miller speak.

00:06:16.442 --> 00:06:19.278 align:start size:94% position:6%
The only Starbucks
Sal would be excited to meet

00:06:19.278 --> 00:06:23.416
are Dirk Benedict
and Katee Sackhoff at Comic-Con.

00:06:35.294 --> 00:06:39.832 size:84% position:42%
He thinks a macchiato,
is the new dance craze.

00:06:46.439 --> 00:06:49.375 align:start size:94% position:6%
Buoy, I meant to say
life preserver,

00:06:49.375 --> 00:06:51.144 align:start size:94% position:6%
I said buoy.

00:06:51.144 --> 00:06:54.814 align:start size:94% position:6%
If you Google image

00:06:54.814 --> 00:06:56.983 align:start size:94% position:6%
lifebuoy, it is
a life preserver,

00:06:56.983 --> 00:06:59.018 align:start size:94% position:6%
but I was just trying
to retrofit.

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:02.355 align:start size:94% position:6%
We got it wrong.

00:07:02.355 --> 00:07:04.257 size:88% position:44%
Oh, this is interesting,
we´ve been talking a lot

00:07:04.257 --> 00:07:05.658
about "Wedding Crashers 2."

00:07:05.658 --> 00:07:08.795 align:start size:94% position:6%
And we were talking a lot,
we wanted credit for it

00:07:08.795 --> 00:07:10.430 size:88% position:44%
because we were talking
about "Wedding Crashers"

00:07:10.430 --> 00:07:11.697 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then all of a sudden
they announced

00:07:11.697 --> 00:07:13.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
that there´s going to be
"Wedding Crashers 2."

00:07:13.132 --> 00:07:18.271
But someone said, hey, man,
you called this a while back.

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:21.307 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now, in 2011,

00:07:21.307 --> 00:07:22.975 size:84% position:42%
I did the White House
Correspondent´s Dinner,

00:07:22.975 --> 00:07:24.677 align:start size:94% position:6%
a night that is often
brought up

00:07:24.677 --> 00:07:26.746 align:start size:94% position:6%
because people say
that is the night

00:07:26.746 --> 00:07:29.215 align:start size:94% position:6%
that Donald Trump decided
to run for president.

00:07:29.215 --> 00:07:34.954
And I´m often asked, do you
regret having told those jokes?

00:07:34.954 --> 00:07:38.224 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I don´t,
but this also happened.

00:07:38.224 --> 00:07:40.059
Let´s take a look at this.

00:07:40.059 --> 00:07:43.095
President and Joe Biden were not
invited to the royal wedding.

00:07:43.095 --> 00:07:44.197
And when Biden found out,

00:07:44.197 --> 00:07:45.932 align:start size:94% position:6%
he immediately said
to the president,

00:07:45.932 --> 00:07:49.735 align:start size:94% position:6%
you, me --
"Wedding Crashers 2."

00:07:52.138 --> 00:07:55.408 size:78% position:39%
So here´s hoping that
for the next decade,

00:07:55.408 --> 00:07:57.443 align:start size:94% position:6%
when I do interviews,
people can say,

00:07:57.443 --> 00:07:58.744 align:start size:94% position:6%
when you look back
at that night,

00:07:58.744 --> 00:08:01.514 align:start size:94% position:6%
do you regret
the "Wedding Crashers 2" joke?

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:07.320
This one breaks my heart.

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:09.322 size:78% position:39%
I called my costar in

00:08:09.322 --> 00:08:10.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Journey to the Center
of the Earth,"

00:08:10.890 --> 00:08:14.727 align:start size:94% position:6%
Brendan Fraser,
Brendan "Frazer."

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:19.131 align:start size:94% position:6%
And in my defense

00:08:19.131 --> 00:08:20.399 align:start size:94% position:6%
the only thing
I´ll say in my defense

00:08:20.399 --> 00:08:24.504 align:start size:94% position:6%
is we were
in insanely close cast.

00:08:24.504 --> 00:08:27.940 size:88% position:44%
Totally first name only.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:29.208 align:start size:94% position:6%
I remember the first day
I was like,

00:08:29.208 --> 00:08:30.676 size:84% position:42%
it´s such a pleasure
to meet you, Mr. Fra --

00:08:30.676 --> 00:08:32.545 align:start size:94% position:6%
and he was like,
"It´s Brendan."

00:08:36.916 --> 00:08:38.851 align:start size:94% position:6%
In these all the stories,
I mean, again,

00:08:38.851 --> 00:08:42.321 size:84% position:42%
there´s been many books
written about that film

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:43.956
and what happened on the set.

00:08:45.958 --> 00:08:50.463 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I do invite you
if you loved that story,

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:53.633 size:81% position:41%
and want to hear more,

00:08:53.633 --> 00:08:57.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
do please read my book
about that time in my life.

00:08:57.570 --> 00:09:00.473 align:start size:94% position:6%
"An actor´s journey
to the center of myself."

00:09:06.078 --> 00:09:08.347 align:start size:94% position:6%
We talked about how
cock a doodle do

00:09:08.347 --> 00:09:10.349 align:start size:94% position:6%
is what a rooster says,
but in German,

00:09:10.349 --> 00:09:12.952
I said it was "kiki leaky."

00:09:12.952 --> 00:09:14.687 align:start size:94% position:6%
A lot of people say
that´s technically right,

00:09:14.687 --> 00:09:15.922
but you´re saying it´s wrong.

00:09:15.922 --> 00:09:17.156
It´s...[ speaks indistinctly ]

00:09:17.156 --> 00:09:20.593 align:start size:94% position:6%
Kiki riki!

00:09:20.593 --> 00:09:22.061 align:start size:94% position:6%
I should have known
that it was like

00:09:22.061 --> 00:09:27.166 align:start size:94% position:6%
the rhythm would be the same,
but it gave me an idea.

00:09:27.166 --> 00:09:32.505
I´m very happy to tell you that
I have pitched this to Pixar.

00:09:32.505 --> 00:09:35.274
It is a children´s film about...

00:09:38.044 --> 00:09:41.213 size:88% position:44%
it´s a World War II film

00:09:41.213 --> 00:09:45.985 align:start size:94% position:6%
where chickens,
American chickens,

00:09:45.985 --> 00:09:49.155
are smuggled into Germany

00:09:49.155 --> 00:09:51.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
so they can spy

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:55.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the German army
who has set up camp at a farm.

00:09:55.962 --> 00:09:59.432 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s thrilling
because the chickens,

00:09:59.432 --> 00:10:02.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
11 hens and one rooster
and by the way,

00:10:02.301 --> 00:10:04.604 align:start size:94% position:6%
the way they smuggle them in
is as fertilized eggs,

00:10:04.604 --> 00:10:06.806
they haven´t even hatched yet.

00:10:06.806 --> 00:10:08.274
It´s just one carton of egg.

00:10:08.274 --> 00:10:10.910 align:start size:94% position:6%
It´s called
the Dirty Dozen and...

00:10:13.479 --> 00:10:16.782
These chickens, they managed
to steal these German secrets

00:10:16.782 --> 00:10:18.951 size:84% position:42%
and then the whole film
is this exciting escape

00:10:18.951 --> 00:10:23.489
across back across enemy lines.

00:10:23.489 --> 00:10:28.027
And all 11 hens make it and
the rooster right at the end,

00:10:28.027 --> 00:10:31.564 align:start size:94% position:6%
who´s disguised
as a German rooster,

00:10:31.564 --> 00:10:34.033
get stopped by border guards

00:10:34.033 --> 00:10:36.569
and he has impeccable German

00:10:36.569 --> 00:10:39.305
because, of course, he´s grew up
there, he was hatched there.

00:10:39.305 --> 00:10:43.743
I don´t need to tell you I´ve
already pitched this to you.

00:10:43.743 --> 00:10:48.180 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he gets away with it,
he convinces them

00:10:48.180 --> 00:10:49.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
that he´s a German rooster
and you,

00:10:49.849 --> 00:10:52.218
as the audience is relieved

00:10:52.218 --> 00:10:57.890
that this night crossing
has not been foiled until

00:10:57.890 --> 00:11:02.395 align:start size:94% position:6%
sun comes up.

00:11:02.395 --> 00:11:06.799
They can´t help themselves,
he´s an American rooster.

00:11:06.799 --> 00:11:11.237 align:start size:94% position:6%
He says, cock a doodle doo
and the jig is up.

00:11:13.606 --> 00:11:17.610 align:start size:94% position:6%
And insofar as his career
as a spy,

00:11:17.610 --> 00:11:20.212 align:start size:94% position:6%
the gig is up.

00:11:20.212 --> 00:11:22.948 align:start size:94% position:6%
Both work.

00:11:22.948 --> 00:11:26.819 align:start size:94% position:6%
And it´s a heartbreaking
final scene

00:11:26.819 --> 00:11:29.088
because you have these 11 hens

00:11:29.088 --> 00:11:32.658 align:start size:94% position:6%
on the allied
hilltop looking down.

00:11:32.658 --> 00:11:38.097 align:start size:94% position:6%
As they lay the rooster´s head
over an old feed sack

00:11:38.097 --> 00:11:40.132 align:start size:94% position:6%
or whatever it is.

00:11:40.132 --> 00:11:44.670 align:start size:94% position:6%
And right before they bring
the ax down,

00:11:44.670 --> 00:11:47.540 align:start size:94% position:6%
he winks at them.

00:11:47.540 --> 00:11:50.109 size:84% position:42%
And then right after
they bring the ax down,

00:11:50.109 --> 00:11:55.181
his headless body just like runs
around for like five minutes

00:11:55.181 --> 00:11:57.850 align:start size:94% position:6%
and that´s the part
Pixar was like, it´s for kids?

00:12:06.425 --> 00:12:08.828 align:start size:94% position:6%
Had a joke about "Metal Gear"
the video game,

00:12:08.828 --> 00:12:10.863 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Metal Gear," cheat codes,
and someone was like,

00:12:10.863 --> 00:12:12.198 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Metal Gear"
didn´t have cheat codes,

00:12:12.198 --> 00:12:13.432 size:78% position:39%
they had Easter eggs.

00:12:13.432 --> 00:12:15.301 align:start size:94% position:6%
And this one broke my heart
because Alex Baze,

00:12:15.301 --> 00:12:17.570 align:start size:94% position:6%
our head writer,

00:12:17.570 --> 00:12:21.640
had written that joke and look,
I´ve said it a bunch,

00:12:21.640 --> 00:12:24.443
Alex Baze is America´s greatest
living joke writer.

00:12:24.443 --> 00:12:26.579 align:start size:94% position:6%
Nothing breaks my heart
more than having to tell him

00:12:26.579 --> 00:12:30.049 align:start size:94% position:6%
he´s made a mistake
and he rarely makes them.

00:12:30.049 --> 00:12:31.450 size:84% position:42%
And he´s very confident

00:12:31.450 --> 00:12:36.489 size:81% position:41%
that the way he writes
a joke is the best way

00:12:36.489 --> 00:12:38.991 align:start size:94% position:6%
to write a joke.

00:12:38.991 --> 00:12:41.260
Other writers say what they´ll
do is they´ll write the jokes

00:12:41.260 --> 00:12:42.528 align:start size:94% position:6%
and then print it out
on a printer

00:12:42.528 --> 00:12:45.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
and they hand it to me
on paper.

00:12:45.464 --> 00:12:47.533
Baze chisels his into rock.

00:12:52.705 --> 00:12:56.876 size:84% position:42%
To go to Baze´s office
and tell him, you know,

00:12:56.876 --> 00:12:58.744
you [bleep] up
because this is top down, right?

00:12:58.744 --> 00:13:00.646 size:81% position:41%
Like we if we´re going
to correct ourselves,

00:13:00.646 --> 00:13:04.850
we have to correct all of us.

00:13:04.850 --> 00:13:07.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I went into his office
and he´s, you know,

00:13:07.186 --> 00:13:10.422 align:start size:94% position:6%
he´s working on the monologue,
so he´s just like...

00:13:13.692 --> 00:13:19.298
And I tell him,
hey, "Metal Gear" doesn´t have,

00:13:19.298 --> 00:13:20.900 align:start size:94% position:6%
you know, they don´t have
cheat codes,

00:13:20.900 --> 00:13:24.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
they have Easter eggs
and he just goes...[ growls ]

00:13:24.603 --> 00:13:28.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
Maybe I should take
my skills elsewhere

00:13:28.808 --> 00:13:31.577
and that -- like we need him,

00:13:31.577 --> 00:13:33.179 align:start size:94% position:6%
like he´s the lifeblood
of this place.

00:13:33.179 --> 00:13:36.582
We could not get by without him.

00:13:36.582 --> 00:13:39.051
And not just as a joke writer

00:13:39.051 --> 00:13:42.021 align:start size:94% position:6%
because he´s been
writing jokes for me.

00:13:42.021 --> 00:13:46.525 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Weekend Update," every single
"Weekend Update" I did.

00:13:46.525 --> 00:13:49.161 align:start size:94% position:6%
He´s the head writer of that
and he came here

00:13:49.161 --> 00:13:51.664
and all these other gigs,

00:13:51.664 --> 00:13:54.233 align:start size:94% position:6%
including the White House
correspondents,

00:13:54.233 --> 00:13:56.502 align:start size:94% position:6%
like, I can´t imagine
what that would have been like

00:13:56.502 --> 00:13:58.637 align:start size:94% position:6%
if I didn´t have
Baze writing jokes.

00:13:58.637 --> 00:14:02.641 align:start size:94% position:6%
And not just,
again, as a joke writer,

00:14:02.641 --> 00:14:06.979
but also a support as someone
who is there for me and, uh,

00:14:06.979 --> 00:14:08.814
I was trying to find that

00:14:08.814 --> 00:14:10.249 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Wedding Crashers 2"
thing today,

00:14:10.249 --> 00:14:12.418
and I actually have never
watched the White House

00:14:12.418 --> 00:14:14.887 align:start size:94% position:6%
Correspondents Dinner
and this really special thing,

00:14:14.887 --> 00:14:17.756 align:start size:94% position:6%
I found this really
special thing, which is,

00:14:17.756 --> 00:14:19.825 align:start size:94% position:6%
I told -- because
I wrote jokes that night, too,

00:14:19.825 --> 00:14:23.863
I told one of my jokes and it --

00:14:23.863 --> 00:14:25.297
it cut to Baze in the audience

00:14:25.297 --> 00:14:29.535 align:start size:94% position:6%
and it wasn´t
the best joke, but,

00:14:29.535 --> 00:14:35.808
I don´t know, it was so touched
by the support I got from Baze.

00:14:35.808 --> 00:14:37.977 align:start size:94% position:6%
You know,
let´s just take a look.

00:14:37.977 --> 00:14:40.713 align:start size:94% position:6%
Comcast, of course,
bought NBC this year,

00:14:40.713 --> 00:14:45.618
I´m assuming by accident or when
Goldman Sachs cut up the network

00:14:45.618 --> 00:14:48.387 align:start size:94% position:6%
and bundled it
in the lower tranche of a CDO.

00:15:03.736 --> 00:15:05.337 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thanks, bro.

00:15:07.640 --> 00:15:11.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
So anyways, I´m backing
out of Baze´s office, right?

00:15:11.210 --> 00:15:12.945 size:78% position:39%
Because I´m terrified
that the last thing

00:15:12.945 --> 00:15:16.715 align:start size:94% position:6%
I want for him to leave
and I say to him,

00:15:16.715 --> 00:15:18.217 align:start size:94% position:6%
"You want me to the door
open or close?"

00:15:18.217 --> 00:15:20.920
And he goes, "Close it
and turn the lights off."

00:15:20.920 --> 00:15:23.756 size:78% position:39%
It´s like, all right,
just leave him there

00:15:23.756 --> 00:15:26.325
in the dark and say, again,
I´m backing up, I´m backing up.

00:15:26.325 --> 00:15:30.296 size:75% position:38%
And then, of course,
who do I bump into?

00:15:30.296 --> 00:15:33.265 align:start size:94% position:6%
Shoemaker is like,

00:15:33.265 --> 00:15:37.670
oh, watch where you´re going.

00:15:37.670 --> 00:15:40.773
And again, I´m like, I´m the one
backing up and he´s facing me.

00:15:40.773 --> 00:15:42.574 align:start size:94% position:6%
But again, I want to have
that conversation

00:15:42.574 --> 00:15:46.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
he goes, "What were you doing
in Baze´s office?"

00:15:46.445 --> 00:15:48.113 align:start size:94% position:6%
There was a correction
saying he goes,

00:15:48.113 --> 00:15:52.651 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Don´t you correct Baze!
We need him."

00:15:52.651 --> 00:15:56.622 align:start size:94% position:6%
Look, I know just sometimes
I don´t need you

00:15:56.622 --> 00:15:57.957
to be in my face all the time.

00:15:57.957 --> 00:16:00.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes, "Oh, what are you
going to do about it?"

00:16:00.459 --> 00:16:04.797 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go, "You know what?
Maybe I´m going to fire you."

00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:08.701 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he goes,
"I got nowhere to go!"

00:16:08.701 --> 00:16:10.336 align:start size:94% position:6%
Just immediate.

00:16:10.336 --> 00:16:12.671 size:81% position:41%
And again, I wanted --

00:16:12.671 --> 00:16:14.606 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was like looking
for some back and forth.

00:16:14.606 --> 00:16:15.941 align:start size:94% position:6%
I had some aggression
to get out.

00:16:15.941 --> 00:16:20.579
But immediately he´s just like,
"No!"

00:16:20.579 --> 00:16:25.651
He´s like, "I don´t know
how to do something else!"

00:16:25.651 --> 00:16:27.886
And now, again, like, now
I´m taking care of him,

00:16:27.886 --> 00:16:30.122 align:start size:94% position:6%
which is the last thing
I wanted to do.

00:16:30.122 --> 00:16:31.557 size:88% position:44%
And I´m like, "Oh, look,

00:16:31.557 --> 00:16:34.693 size:84% position:42%
I´m sure you could do
other stuff, you know?"

00:16:34.693 --> 00:16:37.997
And he´s like, "You think so?"

00:16:37.997 --> 00:16:39.431 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m like, "Yeah."

00:16:39.431 --> 00:16:42.768
He goes, "Well,
there´s one thing I´ve always --

00:16:42.768 --> 00:16:44.603 align:start size:94% position:6%
there´s one thing
I always wanted to do."

00:16:44.603 --> 00:16:46.071 align:start size:94% position:6%
And was like,
"Oh, you know, what is it?"

00:16:46.071 --> 00:16:48.707
He goes, "Oh, it´s crazy."

00:16:48.707 --> 00:16:53.879 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I go, "Look,
I´m sorry I said what I said.

00:16:53.879 --> 00:16:56.915
"But I as much as
I can´t do the show without Baze

00:16:56.915 --> 00:16:58.283
"I can´t do the show without you

00:16:58.283 --> 00:17:01.186 align:start size:94% position:6%
"and anything you
ever wanted to do,

00:17:01.186 --> 00:17:03.555 size:84% position:42%
"I´m sure you could do.

00:17:03.555 --> 00:17:04.890 align:start size:94% position:6%
So why don´t you tell me
what it is."

00:17:04.890 --> 00:17:07.426 align:start size:94% position:6%
He goes, "You sure you´re not
going to make fun of me?"

00:17:07.426 --> 00:17:08.694 align:start size:94% position:6%
I go, "I´m not gonna
make fun of you.

00:17:08.694 --> 00:17:10.562 align:start size:94% position:6%
What is it that you´ve always
wanted to do?"

00:17:10.562 --> 00:17:12.865 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he looks at me
and he goes, "Your mother."

00:17:12.865 --> 00:17:16.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he knows her.

00:17:20.606 --> 00:17:24.243 size:75% position:38%
I´m a little worried
about time tonight.

00:17:24.243 --> 00:17:27.413 align:start size:94% position:6%
I don´t quite know
where we are, but...

00:17:27.413 --> 00:17:29.848 align:start size:94% position:6%
if this averages,
you might have noticed

00:17:29.848 --> 00:17:32.017 align:start size:94% position:6%
the title tonight
it says short form

00:17:34.219 --> 00:17:35.821 align:start size:94% position:6%
because if this average
is between two

00:17:35.821 --> 00:17:38.791 size:88% position:44%
and 20 minutes, it is --

00:17:38.791 --> 00:17:42.361 align:start size:94% position:6%
it is Emmy eligible
in the category of short form.

00:17:42.361 --> 00:17:43.662 align:start size:94% position:6%
Now this ain´t one of
those things

00:17:43.662 --> 00:17:46.298
where I´m here to be like
for your consideration,

00:17:46.298 --> 00:17:48.767 size:75% position:38%
I ain´t that, chief.

00:17:48.767 --> 00:17:51.070 align:start size:94% position:6%
I got an Emmy.

00:17:51.070 --> 00:17:53.906 align:start size:94% position:6%
One.

00:17:53.906 --> 00:17:57.342
Two would be nice for like
then you put books between them.

00:18:02.915 --> 00:18:04.650 size:84% position:42%
But I always I do find,

00:18:04.650 --> 00:18:07.853 align:start size:94% position:6%
like when people are like,
for your consideration,

00:18:07.853 --> 00:18:09.955
I find that a little grotesque.

00:18:09.955 --> 00:18:12.691
So I´m not going to do that.

00:18:12.691 --> 00:18:17.429 align:start size:94% position:6%
I´m only going to say that
with each passing week,

00:18:17.429 --> 00:18:19.932
I remain ambivalent about this.

